{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The portable 5TB drive feels like a useful next purchase because it adds portable backup storage alongside my older 4TB desktop drive, rather than simply repeating what I already have.",
    "The mouse, HDMI cable and USB hub fit my ongoing use of computer peripherals and home entertainment equipment, although I would need a specific replacement or connection need before buying them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older Fire TV sticks offer little after my recent 4K Max bundle purchase, and another Echo speaker does not address a current need alongside my newer Dot and Show 5.",
    "The Show 8's larger screen interests me, but I just bought a Show 5 and its stand. The tablet and wired earbuds have even less connection to a need I currently recognize."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Alexa purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to suggest more Alexa devices, even when they repeat functions I recently added.",
    "My repeated accessory purchases seem to suggest that I always need another mouse, cable or hub, when those purchases depend on a particular practical need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases matter because they can mean a need has just been satisfied; buying a Show 5 stand also suggests I am equipping that device now.",
    "A useful addition matters more to me than surface similarity: portable backup storage adds something to my desktop drive, while a USB 2.0 hub offers less appeal when I already have a USB 3.0 hub."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in home electronics and peripherals but often confuse recently satisfied needs with reasons to buy similar devices again."
}"}
